Spatial navigation: skip offscreen locked subtrees in the candidate walk.

After 0103 the walk still visits every element of the page: 11 672 on a Wikipedia article, about 80 ms of a Down
press on the LG C1. Most of them sit under locked display locks (content-visibility: auto sections away from the
viewport, 54 on that page). ConsiderForBestCandidate() drops offscreen candidates, and a locked subtree that is
offscreen as a whole holds nothing that could win, so the walk now skips such a subtree without checking its
elements. Only while the document is clean (0103's fast path), since IsOffscreen() reads layout. The CandidateWalk
trace event reports skipped_subtrees.

diff --git a/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/spatial_navigation_controller.cc b/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/spatial_navigation_controller.cc
--- a/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/spatial_navigation_controller.cc
